# Captured git diff output, kept exactly as git emitted it. A patch fixture mixes LF
# structural lines with CRLF content lines by design, testing that the parser leaves
# carriage returns alone, so the repository's eol normalization would corrupt the very
# bytes the test asserts on.
#
# This lives here rather than in the root .gitattributes because ktsu.Sdk regenerates the
# root file on every build, which would silently drop the rule.
patch-*.txt -text
